[SIZE=5][B]★ Version History[/B][/SIZE]

[SIZE=4][B]What's New 1.0.0.8[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*]Clickable stations: fixed clicks; the station window shows trains at the station and trains heading there (distance, speed), updates live, click a train to follow it.
[*]Train list per dimension with a counter of trains in other dimensions.
[*]Legend entry for invisible (phantom) tracks.
[*]Readable names for modded / Multiverse dimensions (minecraft:old → Old).
[*]Portals jump to their exit in the other dimension.
[*]Dark scrollbars; wider station window without sideways scrolling.
[*]Website updates load immediately after a plugin update (no stale browser cache).
[/LIST]

[SIZE=4][B]What's New 1.0.0.7[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*][B]Live web map[/B] built into the plugin: tracks with curves, Steam 'n' Rails gauges, portals, stations and smoothly moving trains; train list with search and "follow".
[*][B]Dynmap is optional[/B] — without it the web map and commands keep working.
[*][B]dynmap-stations[/B] / [B]dynmap-trains[/B] switches (both on by default).
[*][B]English / Russian[/B] localization of the website and messages.
[*][B]/railmap[/B] — clickable link built from the address the player used to join.
[*]Blacklists now apply to the web map too.
[*]Existing config.yml files get the new settings appended automatically.
[/LIST]

[SIZE=4][B]What's New 1.0.0.6[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*]Fixed once-per-second server lag spikes: the live scan ran every second on the main thread and repeated slow reflection lookups each time. On hybrid servers such as Youer one scan could freeze the server for 200–470 ms, so trains and mobs stuttered for players. Lookups are now cached and reused, and server API calls are made directly.
[*]Separate update intervals: trains are updated every 5 seconds and stations every 60 seconds by default (train-update-interval-seconds and station-update-interval-seconds).
[*]Change-only marker updates: a marker is only touched when its position, name or description actually changes.
[*]Faster blacklist handling: blacklist files are checked once per update instead of once per marker.
[*]Stale marker cleanup fixed: removed stations and trains now disappear from the map (train markers after 3 missed updates).
[/LIST]

[SIZE=4][B]What's New 1.0.0.5[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*]NeoForge 1.21.1 (Build 265) compatibility fix: fixed the startup crash caused by an IllegalArgumentException / argument type mismatch. The task scheduler now uses direct BukkitScheduler calls instead of reflection, ensuring stable operation on NeoForge 21.1.265 and earlier versions.
[/LIST]

[SIZE=4][B]What's New 1.0.0.4[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*]Configurable file export interval: added export-interval-seconds (default: 3600 s) to control how often stations.txt and trains.txt are written.
[*]Performance optimization: separated live Dynmap marker scans from background file export timers to reduce disk I/O.
[*]Comment preservation: config.yml keeps all helpful comments and icon listings.
[/LIST]

[SIZE=4][B]What's New 1.0.0.3[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*]Automatic train list export (trains.txt) to plugins/Create-Railways-Dynmap-Bridge/trains.txt.
[*]New command /gettrains (permission create.stations.admin) to print the list and count of all trains in chat or console.
[/LIST]

[SIZE=4][B]What's New 1.0.0.2[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*]Automatic station export (stations.txt), one station name per line.
[*]New command /getstations (permission create.stations.admin) to view the list and count of all stations in chat or console.
[/LIST]

[SIZE=4][B]What's New in Version 1.0.0.1[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*]Full integration between the Create railway system and Dynmap.
[*]Track layout and station mapping.
[*]Real-time train location markers.
[*]Customizable station and train icons.
[*]Automatic dimension tracking and world matching, with manual overrides.
[*]Live status updates for operating trains and stations.
[/LIST]
